 in this mess and I  would argue that the American public  does not want this well I would also  point to you know aside from the  constitutional legality and  international law angles this is setting  the u.s. and Iran on a potential  collision course and this is where I  believe Donald Trump is the greatest  risk lots of stuff  can be undone if Trump lasts until 2020  many of the executive orders that are  more symbolic in nature those can be  undone if Donald Trump even manages to  get in sort of on the path to approval  and activation some health care plan and  we'll talk about that later in the show  that can take a very long time and much  of it might still be able to be undone  if Donald Trump leaves office in 2020 or  shortly before who knows what the  scenario would be Donald Trump is so  erratic done on any particular day he  might end up bombing this country or  that leader or this other group he might  make an irreversible decision involving  military force and really do something  nuts and I don't know if it's in North  Korea the serious situation the  involvement of Iran  that's what's scariest about Trump right  I mean with a lot of these diplomatic or  domestic issues I think you know if he  has a four year presidency by the next  president if it is a Democrat those  things can be undone the example may be  getting back into the Paris climate deal  tour but I mean if you're messing with  the Middle East that could have  ramifications that last for decades
 

